section: rts
synopsis: Fix numerous minor issues in posix signal handling
description:
  Many uses of posix signal masks were wrong or usless, especially in the
  threaded RTS. This may fix a number of issues noticed on macOS where signal
  masks got messed up, including when creating child processes.

  Signal delivery was racy in the non-threaded RTS which could allow signals
  to not be delivered for extended periods of time.

  Signal handlers were also calling functions which were not guaranteed to be
  safe to use from signal handlers (which in principle can lead to lockups or
  data corruption). Unfortunately the SIGQUIT handler that dumps a DWARF-based
  stack trace has had to be disabled, until we can figure out how to do this
  safely from a signal handler. See issue #28071.
